To achieve the desired functionality of displaying an image with a caption on a web page using HTML and CSS, we will follow these steps:

1. Create a basic structure for the webpage including the `head` section where we define the title and styles, and the `body` section where we place our content.

2. Within the `body`, we'll use a `div` element with the ID "img-container". This container will hold both the image and the caption.

3. The image should be centered within its parent div, and styled appropriately (e.g., with maximum width and aspect ratio).

4. Below the image, we add a paragraph containing the caption. We also ensure that the paragraph is aligned properly.

5. Finally, we apply hyperlinks around the image so users can navigate directly to any external pages associated with the images.

Here's how your complete HTML file might look:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Image with Caption</title>
  <style>
    body { 
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif; 
      line-height: 1.6; 
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      background-color: #f4f4f9;
    }

    .container {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 100vh;
    }

    #img-container {
      text-align: center;
    }

    #img-container img {
      max-width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    #img-container p {
      margin: 0;
      color: white;
      font-size: 1.2em;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      position: absolute;
      bottom: -2rem;
      left: 50%;
      transform: translateX(-50%);
      z-index: 1;
    }

    #caption-text {
      background-color: #007bff;
      color: white;
      padding: 0.5rem;
      border-radius: 4px;
      text-align: center;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    a:hover,
    a:focus {
      outline: none;
    }

    @media screen and (max-width: 768px) {
      .container {
        flex-direction: column;
      }

      #img-container {
        text-align: left;
      }

      #img-container img {
        max-width: 100%;
        height: auto;
      }

      #img-container p {
        bottom: 1rem;
        left: calc(50% - 15rem);
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="container">
  <div id="img-container">
    <a href="https://www.example.com/">
      <img src="https://example.com/image.jpg" alt="Example Image">
    </a>
    <p id="caption-text">This is the caption for the example image.</p>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

